## Description

Generated public ports are currently stable only in a few special cases, which means endpoint addresses can change across AppHost restarts and linked Git worktrees require explicit isolation. This change introduces a consistent persistent port model for both C# and polyglot AppHosts.

Generated public ports are stored in an AppHost-local key/value state file under `.aspire/state`. The state store uses cross-process locking, atomic replacement, per-value schema versioning, and a product-owned `.gitignore`. Port allocation continues to treat executable target ports as transient, while preserving generated public ports that form the user-observable endpoint identity.

The implementation also:

- migrates existing `Resources:<resource>:<endpoint>:port` user-secret values when first encountered, without writing new allocations back to user secrets
- adds `features.gitWorktreeIsolationEnabled` to automatically use isolated mode for AppHosts in linked Git worktrees, while preserving explicit `--isolated true|false` precedence
- adds `portAllocation.persistInIsolatedMode` so isolated runs can opt into stable persisted ports
- projects the AppHost-relative port policy consistently into managed C# and polyglot AppHosts

