Part 4 of the `beacon mcp connect` series. The library (Asymptote-Labs/agent-beacon#692) and the commands (Asymptote-Labs/agent-beacon#693) are merged, so this PR now targets `main`.

## What

- **New `docs/cli/mcp-connect.mdx`** covers:
  - `connect`, `disconnect` and `status`;
  - how the URL is resolved and checked;
  - how files are edited, backed up and recorded;
  - OAuth versus `--token-env`;
  - the entry and sign-in step for each harness;
  - the harnesses set up by hand;
  - the 4 KB and Metadata-only limits on what Beacon Managed MCP can find.

  The page is added to `docs/docs.json` under the `beacon mcp` group.
- **`docs/cli/mcp.mdx`** gains a "Local and Beacon Managed servers" table: `beacon` is the local server, `beacon-managed` is Beacon Managed. The tool list is now marked as the local server's, and the local-only note names `connect` as the one command that makes a network request, and only when you run it.
- **`docs/cli/mcp-doctor.mdx`** gains a "Client configuration" section explaining that the printed entry is the local `beacon` server.
- **`docs/cli/index.mdx`** lists `connect`, `disconnect` and `status`.
- **README** gets a short `beacon mcp connect` note under "Explore your history".
- **CLAUDE.md** gets a Telemetry Scope entry for the command.
- **`beacon mcp doctor` output** now says `"beacon"` is the local server and points at `beacon mcp connect` for `"beacon-managed"`. The `beacon mcp` group also gets a `Long` description.
